{"text":"Approved tech stack pinned in STACK.md. Single source of truth for which tools/frameworks/versions this repo uses. Drives CLAUDE.md tech-stack section. Tool-agnostic context hub: any agent reading markdown picks up the constraints (Claude Code, Cursor, Continue, Aider, Codex CLI). Future Step 2/3 dependency additions must go through STACK.md amendment + bd decision record.","tags":["stack","context-hub","decisions","versions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-07","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard and any project that wants the same pattern"}
{"text":"Package manager: npm (not yarn or pnpm). Operator consensus 2026-05-07; secondary developer prefers npm; npm 10 workspaces are mature; pnpm/yarn-berry adoption is uneven. Lockfile is package-lock.json (committed).","tags":["npm","package-manager","decisions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-07","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
{"text":"Node version manager: any tool that reads .nvmrc (nvm, fnm, volta, n). The repo pins .nvmrc 22.12.0; pick whichever manager the operator already has. Don't mix two on the same machine.","tags":["nvm","node-version","decisions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-07","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
{"text":"Sessions-spike v4 write API: extend the existing packages/server (Fastify 5); do NOT add Go or a separate server. The monorepo is uniformly TypeScript with shared Zod types (@metaswarm-dashboard/types) and one vitest/coverage/eslint apparatus; a second language fragments the toolchain and breaks type-sharing for a handful of write endpoints. Go was floated by the operator and the choice explicitly delegated to the executor: evaluated and rejected.","tags":["stack","go-rejected","fastify","sessions-spike-v4","decisions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-17","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
{"text":"Sessions-spike v4: the dashboard becomes read-WRITE, scoped strictly to its own datalake (METASWARM_DASHBOARD_DATA_DIR). Observed host repos stay strictly read-only — the zero-footprint-on-host-repos invariant is unchanged. Operator session ratings and snapshots are written into the datalake via Fastify endpoints. Supersedes the v3 read-only-SPA MVP stance; the SPA write-ban lint rule is re-scoped (SPA may POST only to the dashboard's own API).","tags":["architecture","read-write","datalake","sessions-spike-v4","decisions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-17","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
{"text":"Sessions-spike v4 error-handling rubric scorer rewritten to a single complementary handled/unhandled definition (design §5). A tool-error at index i is UNHANDLED iff events[i+1] is a tool-use whose (toolName, summary) equals the errored call's (the nearest preceding tool-use) — a blind identical retry — OR no event follows i (session ended on the error). HANDLED is the exact complement, so every error is deterministically classified. Verdict on handled/total ratio: >=0.8 pass, 0.5-0.8 watch, <0.5 fail, 0 errors na. Rationale: v3's rule scored an error 'handled' only if a Read/Grep tool-use or assistant-text followed within 2 events, so the WU-4.5 calibration found competent sessions that investigated via a diagnostic Bash (git status, ls) were wrongly failed. Limitation: summary is truncated to <=200 chars, so two distinct calls with an identical 200-char prefix compare as equal — accepted, the rubric is advisory not an oracle (anti-goal §12.9).","tags":["rubric","error-handling","threshold-change","sessions-spike-v4","calibration","decisions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-17","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
{"text":"Sessions-spike v4 thrashing rubric scorer rewritten to a >=3-edit-run rule (design §5). A thrash run is a maximal run of >=3 Edit tool-use events to the same file path, each <5000ms after the previous Edit of the run, with no Read tool-use of that same path between two consecutive edits. Verdict on the run count: 0 pass, 1 watch, >=2 fail (no na). Rationale: v3's rule counted every adjacent same-file <5s Edit pair as an 'episode' and fired watch at a single pair, so the WU-4.5 calibration found normal 'edit section A then edit section B of the same file' tripped it; the >=3-run bar fixes the false positive (anti-goal §12.9).","tags":["rubric","thrashing","threshold-change","sessions-spike-v4","calibration","decisions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-17","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
{"text":"Sessions-spike v4 calibration model: the process rubric is ADVISORY, not a gate. ProcessRubricScore.overall is informational only — it never blocks or scores a session. The operator's SessionRating (recorded via the SPA survey) is the ground truth; calibration is continuous — each rating records per-KPI agreement/disagreement with the rubric's suggestion, aggregated into CalibrationSummary (N>=5 sample floor). Rationale: the WU-4.5 calibration (N=2, agent-judged independently from events before seeing the rubric) found the rubric non-discriminating on real ~/.claude/projects transcripts, so v3's gate-the-session stance was killed (docs/sessions-calibration.md §15.3) and v4 pivoted to operator-rated, rubric-as-suggestion.","tags":["calibration","rubric","advisory","sessions-spike-v4","architecture","decisions"],"recorded_at":"2026-05-18","applies_to":"metaswarm-dashboard"}
